iddleware","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoMiddleware"],"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true},{"anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BoundedResponse","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/FlushOutcome"],"title":"Enumerations","generated":true},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Foundation"],"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Swidux-logo","type":"image"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The dispatch cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Companion-Packages","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Companion Packages"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their own repositories so a third-party SDK never enters the core dependency graph. Each ships a drop-in service conformer plus a preview mock, and publishes its own DocC reference:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — RevenueCat adapter for the paywall plugin ("},{"code":"RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":", and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"type":"text","text":" sheet). See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/"},{"type":"text","text":" — Mixpanel adapter for the analytics plugin ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":"). See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference"},{"text":"